        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define outcomes and their probabilities\n    sales = [70, 40, 25]\n    probabilities = [0.05, 0.70, 0.25]\n\n    # Calculate the probability-weighted mean and population variance\n    mean_sales = sum(value * probability for value, probability in zip(sales, probabilities))\n    variance = sum(\n        probability * (value - mean_sales) ** 2\n        for value, probability in zip(sales, probabilities)\n    )\n    answer = round(variance ** 0.5, 3)\n\n    # Return the standard deviation in millions of dollars\n    return answer\n```",
